{
  "book": "1CO",
  "chapter": 13,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "1",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.1",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.1"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.1"
        },
        {
          "text": "If I should speak in the tongues of men and of angels, but have not love, I have become a sounding brass or a clanging cymbal.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.1",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.1"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "2",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.2",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.2"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.2"
        },
        {
          "text": "And if I should have prophecy and should understand all mysteries and all knowledge, and if I should have all faith so as to remove mountains, but have not love, I am nothing.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.2",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.2"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "3",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.3",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.3"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.3"
        },
        {
          "text": "And if I should give away all my possessions, and if I should deliver up my body that I may boast, but have not love, I am profited nothing.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.3",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.3"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "4",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.4",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.4"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.4"
        },
        {
          "text": "Love is patient, it is kind; love does not envy, love does not boast, it is not puffed up.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.4",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.4"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "5",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.5",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.5"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.5"
        },
        {
          "text": "It does not act unbecomingly, it does not seek its own [things], it is not provoked, it keeps no reckoning of evil.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.5",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.5"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "6",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.6",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.6"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.6"
        },
        {
          "text": "It does not rejoice at unrighteousness, but it rejoices with the truth.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.6",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.6"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "7",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.7",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.7"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.7"
        },
        {
          "text": "It bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, endures all things.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.7",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.7"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.7"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "8",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.8",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.8"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.8"
        },
        {
          "text": "Love never fails; but if [there are] prophecies, they will be made null; and if [there are] tongues, they will cease; and if [there is] knowledge, it will be made null.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.8",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.8"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.8"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "9",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.9",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.9"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.9"
        },
        {
          "text": "For we know in part and we prophesy in part;",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.9",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.9"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "10",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.10",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.10"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.10"
        },
        {
          "text": "but when the perfect should come, the partial will be made null.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.10",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.10"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.10"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "11",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.11",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.11"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.11"
        },
        {
          "text": "When I was a child, I was speaking like a child, I was thinking like a child, I was reasoning like a child; when I became a man, I have made null the [things] of the child.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.11",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.11"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "12",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.12",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.12"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.12"
        },
        {
          "text": "For now we see through a glass in obscurity, but then, face to face. Now I know in part, but then I will know fully, even as I have been fully known.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.12",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.12"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.12"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "verse",
      "role": "scripture",
      "sourceId": "",
      "runs": [
        {
          "verse": "13",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.13",
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.13"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.13"
        },
        {
          "text": "But now these three things remain: faith, hope, love; but the greatest of these [is] love.",
          "anchor": "1CO.13.13",
          "marks": [],
          "anchors": [
            "1CO.13.13"
          ],
          "sourceAnchor": "1CO.13.13"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
